    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0038" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760D.62/91</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-06">May 6, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Finnish Minister called in company with his Counselor.<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d37-f1"/> He said that his country was much concerned about the
                    report that some twelve thousand German troops had moved into a certain area of
                    Finland; that he desired to deny this most emphatically, as he desired also to
                    deny a number of other rumors and reports about special relations between his
                    country and Germany. I stated that we had not accepted any of these reports here
                    at the State Department; that we never accepted damaging reports against a
                    friendly country like Finland without full confirmation in the first place, and
                    that we have treated lightly these reports to which he referred. He seemed very
                    much relieved at this, but urged that more publicity be given by us in denial,
                    especially the report about the German troop occupation. I requested him to call
                    on Mr. McDermott<anchor n="73" xml:id="d37-f2"/> and go over this phase, which
                    he said he would be glad to do.</p>
                <p>The Minister expressed great appreciation at the aid we are giving Finland.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
